-- title:
--   Pro-representing object determined by its functor on Artinian test algebras
-- statement:
--   Let $\Lambda$ be a commutative ring, and let $R_1$ and $R_2$ be commutative rings in a single universe, each local, Noetherian, adically complete with respect to its maximal ideal, and each equipped with a $\Lambda$-algebra structure such that the composite of the structure map $\Lambda \to R_i$ with the residue map $R_i \to R_i/\mathfrak m_i$ is surjective, i.e. the residue field of $R_i$ is generated by the image of $\Lambda$. Suppose given data $\eta$ assigning to every local Artinian commutative $\Lambda$-algebra $T$ (in the same universe) whose residue field is likewise reached from $\Lambda$, i.e. for which $\Lambda \to T \to T/\mathfrak m_T$ is surjective, a bijection $\eta_T \colon \mathrm{Hom}_{\Lambda\text{-alg}}(R_1, T) \simeq \mathrm{Hom}_{\Lambda\text{-alg}}(R_2, T)$, and suppose these bijections are natural in the following sense: for all such test algebras $T$, $T'$, every $\Lambda$-algebra map $f \colon T \to T'$ and every $\Lambda$-algebra map $g \colon R_1 \to T$, one has $\eta_{T'}(f \circ g) = f \circ \eta_T(g)$. Then the type of $\Lambda$-algebra isomorphisms $R_1 \simeq R_2$ is nonempty.
--
--   This is the uniqueness part of pro-representability in the style of Schlessinger's theory of functors of Artin rings: a complete Noetherian local $\Lambda$-algebra with residue field generated by $\Lambda$ is determined up to $\Lambda$-isomorphism by the functor it represents on local Artinian test algebras, naturality being required for all $\Lambda$-algebra maps of test algebras, not merely surjections. It is used to identify completed local rings arising on modular curves with explicit presentations of the form $S[X]/(g)$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_IsLocalRing_nonempty_algEquiv_of_forall_isArtinianRing_algHom_equiv.lean

